<title>USA: Fremont to buy Xerox unit.</title>
<headline>Fremont to buy Xerox unit.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA MONICA, Calif. 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fremont General Corp said Monday it signed a definitive agreement with Talegen Holdings Inc, a subsidiary of Xerox Corp, to purchase Industrial Indemnity Holdings Inc.</p>
<p>Fremont will pay Talegen $365 million in cash and pay off a $79 million outstanding debt obligation that Industrial Indemnity has to Talegen, a statement issued by Fremont said.</p>
<p>Xerox issued a statement saying the purchase price is in excess of book value and is consistent with the estimated value of the unit when Xerox discontinued its insurance operations in 1995.</p>
</text>
